    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ccb26020_beccbc5b",
        "filename": "driver/wpc/cps8100.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 391,
      "author": {
        "id": 1544342
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-10T09:00:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because cps8100_get_alert_info() is the first function called by peripheral_charger driver, so we need to probe in cps8100_get_alert_info()\n\nWhen CPS8x00 is powered on or reset, IRQ will be fired to the peripheral_charger driver, peripheral_charger driver calls get_event() and cps8100_get_alert_info() get called to get the alert info of CPS8x00, so peripheral_charger knows that cps8x00 CPS is just out of reset then cps8100_init() will be called \n\nCode flow is here:\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/peripheral_charger.c;l\u003d445",
      "parentUuid": "4433c725_c52e4e7d",
